    {
      "text": "Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) is the standard markup language[a] for documents designed to be displayed in a web browser. It defines the content and structure of web content. It",
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwEg"
    },
    {
      "text": "HTML documents are required to start with a document type declaration (informally, a \"doctype\"). In browsers, the doctype helps to define the rendering mode—particularly whether to",
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwBY0"
    },
    {
      "text": "WYSIWYG editors remain a controversial topic because of their perceived flaws such as:",
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwByY"
    },
    {
      "text": "<!DOCTYPE html> <html> <head> <title>This is a title</title> </head> <body> <div> <p>Hello world!</p> </div> </body> </html>",
      "tag": "PRE",
      "id": "mwAlU"
    },
    {
